---
import ContentLayout from "../layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
---

<ContentLayout
  title="Privacy | Stream Mix"
  description="Understand what Stream Mix stores in your browser and how embedded Twitch, YouTube, and Kick players interact with third-party services."
  heading="Privacy"
>
  <p>
    Stream Mix does not require an account and does not use behavioral analytics
    or advertising trackers. Your mixer configuration is stored in your browser
    so it can be restored when you return.
  </p>

  <h2>Information stored locally</h2>
  <p>
    Stream Mix uses localStorage to save the channels or video IDs you add,
    their display modes, grid positions, and interface preferences. This data
    remains on your device unless you clear your browser storage. It is not sent
    to a Stream Mix server.
  </p>

  <h2>Embedded third-party services</h2>
  <p>
    When you add a stream, your browser connects directly to the selected
    platform. Twitch, YouTube, or Kick may process network information, set
    cookies, or apply their own privacy policies while serving video and chat.
    Stream Mix does not control those services.
  </p>

  <h2>Shared workspace links</h2>
  <p>
    When you use the share button, Stream Mix encodes the stream identifiers,
    display modes, and grid positions in the link’s URL fragment. This happens
    in your browser and is not uploaded to a Stream Mix server. Anyone who
    receives the link can read and open the workspace it contains.
  </p>

  <h2>Error monitoring</h2>
  <p>
    Stream Mix uses Sentry in production to receive technical reports when the
    application fails. Reports can include an error message, stack trace,
    browser and operating-system details, recent technical breadcrumbs, and
    network information used to deliver the report. Stream Mix removes URL query
    strings and fragments, request headers, request bodies, cookies, and user
    fields before sending an event. Session replay, performance tracing, and
    analytics are not enabled. See <a
      href="https://sentry.io/privacy/"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noreferrer">Sentry’s privacy policy</a
    > for information about Sentry’s processing.
  </p>

  <h2>Removing saved layouts</h2>
  <p>
    Remove individual streams using their window controls, or clear the site’s
    stored data through your browser settings to reset the entire layout and all
    preferences.
  </p>

  <p><em>Last updated: August 2, 2026.</em></p>
</ContentLayout>
